# Cloudflare Pages routing — hides internal paths from public and forwards
# the API + SSE stream to the hosted backend.
#
# On Cloudflare Pages you upload `docs/` as the site root and set the
# custom domain to proofvisor.com. Pages inherits Cloudflare's global
# edge network — unlimited bandwidth, HTTP/3, Brotli, automatic Argo.
#
# Free tier: 500 builds/month, unlimited bandwidth, unlimited requests.
# Zero rebuild cost when compared to Vercel/Netlify. No lock-in — the
# static site is the same directory you would rsync anywhere.
#
# _redirects syntax: <source> <dest> [status] [!Header=…]
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# API proxy — keeps the console and API on the same origin so cookies
# work with SameSite=Lax and no CORS preflight is needed. Change the
# right-hand side to point at your API host (Render, Cloud Run, Koyeb).
#
# DISABLED. The hosted API is live on Render at
# https://api.proofvisor.com (CNAME to agentvisor-api.onrender.com), and
# the site itself is on GitHub Pages, which ignores this file anyway. On any host that honors this
# file the /api/* rule would also SHADOW /api/ — which on the current
# site is the rustdoc export (a working, link-crawled page). Before
# re-enabling both lines: confirm api.proofvisor.com resolves and
# move the rustdoc to /docs/api/ first.
# /api/*  https://api.proofvisor.com/api/:splat  200
# /healthz  https://api.proofvisor.com/healthz  200

# Short-link aliases. NOTE: the site currently deploys to GitHub
